<div id="ClsNeeraProblem-{{ section.id }}" class="cls-neera-problem">
  <div class="cls-neera-problem__inner">
    <div class="cls-neera-problem__content">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="cls-neera-problem__heading cls-neera-type-heading">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.paragraph_1 != blank -%}
        <div class="cls-neera-problem__paragraph cls-neera-type-body">{{ section.settings.paragraph_1 }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.paragraph_2 != blank -%}
        <div class="cls-neera-problem__paragraph cls-neera-type-body">{{ section.settings.paragraph_2 }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.paragraph_3 != blank -%}
        <div class="cls-neera-problem__paragraph cls-neera-type-body">{{ section.settings.paragraph_3 }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="cls-neera-problem__photo">
      {%- if section.settings.photo_image != blank -%}
        <img
          src="{{ section.settings.photo_image | image_url: width: 900 }}"
          srcset="{{ section.settings.photo_image | image_url: width: 450 }} 450w, {{ section.settings.photo_image | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w, {{ section.settings.photo_image | image_url: width: 1280 }} 1280w"
          sizes="(min-width: 768px) 560px, 100vw"
          alt="{{ section.settings.photo_image.alt | default: section.settings.heading | escape }}"
          loading="lazy"
        >
      {%- else -%}
        <img
          src="{{ section.settings.photo_image_fallback | asset_url }}"
          srcset="{{ section.settings.photo_image_fallback | replace: '.jpg', '-450.jpg' | asset_url }} 450w, {{ section.settings.photo_image_fallback | replace: '.jpg', '-900.jpg' | asset_url }} 900w, {{ section.settings.photo_image_fallback | asset_url }} 1280w"
          sizes="(min-width: 768px) 560px, 100vw"
          alt="{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}"
          loading="lazy"
        >
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Neera the problem",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "What if it isn’t your age?"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "paragraph_1",
      "label": "Paragraph 1",
      "default": "<p>Many of us quietly accept afternoon fog, a restless gut, and persistent <strong>low-level inflammation</strong> as the price of getting older. Yet there is another factor most people <strong>never examine:</strong> the container they drink from every day for decades.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "paragraph_2",
      "label": "Paragraph 2",
      "default": "<p>Plastic bottles can shed microplastics and compounds such as <strong>BPA</strong> and phthalates into the water. <strong>Even high-quality</strong> stainless steel develops microscopic scratches over time — places where bacteria can settle and multiply. <strong>Aluminum bottles</strong> often hide a thin liner that eventually wears. <strong>Copper is different.</strong> For centuries, water stored in pure copper vessels was part of daily life in <strong>Ayurvedic</strong> tradition. Not because it was trendy, but because the material itself behaves differently.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "paragraph_3",
      "label": "Paragraph 3",
      "default": "<p>This is not a <strong>“promise”</strong> that one bottle will erase every symptom. It is an invitation to remove one constant source of plastic and chemical exposure and replace it with a <strong>vessel</strong> that has been used for water storage for thousands of years — now made for modern life.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Photo"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "photo_image",
      "label": "Photo"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "photo_image_fallback",
      "label": "Photo fallback asset",
      "default": "neera-problem-bottles.jpg"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Neera the problem"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
